==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|σῆψις||putrefaction}}, from {{m|grc|σήπειν||to make rotten}}, from {{m|grc|σήψ||a kind of lizard, also a kind of serpent whose bite was alleged to cause putrefaction}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sepses}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} A serious medical [[condition]] in which the whole body is inflamed, and a known or suspected infection is present.

